# Flutter Development Rules - Comprehensive Guide

## 🎯 Core Principles

- **🚨 CRITICAL: Always use explicit colours** - Never rely on Material Design defaults (Android 13 compatibility)
- **🚫 NEVER RUN THE APP** - The developer will always run the app themselves; AI should never execute `flutter run` or attempt to launch the application
- **Always use British English spellings** (colour, centre, organisation, etc.)
- **Extract Complex Build Methods** using `_buildXXX()` pattern
- **Separate Business Logic** from UI rendering
- **Use Centralised Styling** from `lib/styles/`
- **Follow Consistent Naming** conventions throughout
- **Test Everything** - All new widgets must have tests
- **Quality Assurance** - Always run Flutter Analyze and tests after changes

